11. THE ASSISTANT PANELS

Four optional panels (watch-along, chat, concierge, paced commentary) talk to two
local services on this PC: a speech and commentary server (127.0.0.1:8899) and a
local model server (127.0.0.1:1234). They can both be absent. The panels hold
pick-lists (model, voice, persona, speech engine, interval), start and stop buttons,
a message field, and several free-text fields that the owner has filled in.
Rules: design the frame only. Every free-text field and every configured text is the
owner's content: keep it exactly, never rewrite, shorten or pre-fill it, and in
mock-ups draw it as a grey block labelled "existing text, unchanged". Personas are
read-only here. Do not add filters, warnings or disclaimers.


14. A STAND-IN FOR PREVIEWING WITHOUT THE APP

To run your components in a browser, define this before your code loads. It returns
neutral placeholder data only. Extend it as you need more of section 10.

  const clip = (n, scripted) => ({
    videoPath: 'D:/library/clip_' + n + '.mp4', name: 'clip_' + n + '.mp4',
    scriptPath: scripted ? 'D:/library/clip_' + n + '.funscript' : undefined,
    hasFunscript: scripted, durationMs: 180000 + n * 7000, strokes: scripted ? 400 + n : 0,
    spm: scripted ? 120 + (n % 60) : 0, avgSpeed: scripted ? 180 + (n % 90) : 0,
    sizeBytes: 300e6, createdAt: Date.now() - n * 864e5, addedAt: Date.now() - n * 36e5,
    width: [1280, 1920, 3840][n % 3], height: [720, 1080, 2160][n % 3], contentKind: 'unknown',
  });
  const wait = (ms, v) => new Promise((r) => setTimeout(() => r(v), ms));
  const script = { version: '1.0', actions: Array.from({ length: 400 }, (_, i) =>
    ({ at: i * 450, pos: i % 2 ? 90 - (i % 7) * 5 : 10 + (i % 5) * 4 })) };
  window.electronAPI = new Proxy({
    scanDirectories: () => wait(300, Array.from({ length: 2000 }, (_, i) => clip(i + 1, i % 3 !== 0))),
    listScriptVersions: (p) => wait(50, [{ label: 'default', path: p }, { label: 'v2', path: p }]),
    getFunscript: () => wait(80, script),
    getThumbnail: () => wait(120, null), getThumbnailCached: () => wait(10, null),
    getResumeAll: () => wait(20, {}), setResume: () => wait(5),
    connectHandy: (key) => wait(12000, key ? { connected: true, api: 'v3', fw: '4.0.0' }
                                              : { connected: false, error: 'Connection key is required' }),
    uploadHandyScript: () => wait(2000, { success: true }),
    playHandy: () => wait(900), pauseHandy: () => wait(900), syncHandyTime: () => wait(900),
    liveTameGet: () => wait(10, { pace: 100, speed: 100, length: 100, vibe: 0 }),
    listPatterns: () => wait(60, [{ folder: 'Pattern set A', name: 'Pattern 1', path: 'p1' }]),
    myTagsGet: () => wait(40, { 'Playlist 1': [] }), playlistsGet: () => wait(40, {}),
  }, { get: (t, k) => t[k] || (String(k).startsWith('on') ? () => () => {} : () => wait(50, null)) });

Note the 12-second connectHandy: it is deliberate. Design for it.


